# Wireworm — Showcase

The finished game ships a showcase: the store-page presentation a player reads
before deciding to play. It is a `showcase/` directory at the root of this
repository, committed with the rest of the project, holding a description of the
game and a short carousel of captured media. This file defines its contents.

## Layout

Every file of the showcase sits directly in `showcase/`, with no subdirectories:

- `showcase/showcase.md`, the description.
- `showcase/showcase.toml`, the carousel.
- The media files the carousel and the description name.

## The description

`showcase/showcase.md` is Markdown written for a player: what Wireworm is, how a
descent is fought, and what makes the charged field worth playing around. Three
to five short paragraphs. It is strictly about playing the game; implementation,
architecture, and tooling stay out of it. It may embed images that sit beside it,
referenced by bare relative path (for example `![The board](board.png)`); every
image it embeds is a `.png` in `showcase/`.

## The carousel

`showcase/showcase.toml` lists the media in the order they are presented, one
`[[media]]` table per entry:

{{#if (eq engine.slug "none")}}
```toml
[[media]]
file = "discharge.webm"
name = "A chain-arc discharge clearing a charged cluster"

[[media]]
file = "title.png"
name = "The title screen"
```
{{else}}
```toml
[[media]]
file = "discharge.json.gz"
name = "A chain-arc discharge clearing a charged cluster"

[[media]]
file = "title.png"
name = "The title screen"
```
{{/if}}

- `file` names a file directly in `showcase/`, with no path separators. Every
  file the carousel names exists there, and each stays under 25 MiB.
- `name` is a caption of a few words.
- The carousel holds two to four entries. The first entry leads, so it carries
  the strongest view of live play.

## Media

{{#if (eq engine.slug "none")}}
The file extension states what an entry is:

| Extension | Media |
| --- | --- |
| `.png` | A screenshot of the running game. |
| `.webm` | A video clip of the running game, a few seconds long. |

Screenshots carry most of the carousel. Where motion is worth showing, such as
the worm winding down a charged field or a discharge arcing through a cluster, a
short `.webm` clip carries it; how screenshots and clips are captured is the
build's own business.
{{else}}
The file extension states what an entry is:

| Extension | Media |
| --- | --- |
| `.png` | A screenshot of the running game. |
| `.json.gz` | A replay: a gzipped recording of the game's own drawing, made with the engine's recorder. |
| `.webm` | A video clip. |

Anything in motion is captured as a replay rather than a video.

## Capturing a replay

A replay is a gzipped JSON recording made with the engine's recorder, which the
engine documents in `engine/recording.md` at the root of this repository. Each
replay holds a few seconds of live play, such as the worm winding down a charged
field or a discharge arcing through a cluster, rather than a menu. How
screenshots and replays are captured is the build's own business.
{{/if}}

Everything a showcase entry shows arises from the game's own rules under real
play. Posing an outcome through the debug surface is not a capture of the game.
